{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact scale-runner head 06b9f39876a9fb8aa5c03ef348a395e638177407 on builder/scale-runner-20261109, tree cef76a6e, all 15 artifacts, for request a5f3d838 under promise 2f8e7382, ruling 38d61076 and review request c4c9dd65. My promise fcf5d706 left the head blank through a shell error in its text. This verdict binds the exact head above. Only the main scale workflow sets a deadline factor of three, and every local and review deadline stays as it was.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 9ce45bd1 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 15 paths that its artifacts cover, and the note is the primary artifact. The commit-message check passes: 4 checked, 0 flagged. No product source, dependency, lockfile, seal or Wrangler file changes.\n- The owners. I removed the helper import and the `scaleDeadline(...)` wrapper from each of the four owners. Each result is byte-equal to main 9ce45bd1. No body, entry count, bound or assertion changes.\n- The factor. `scaleDeadlineFactor` accepts only a positive integer and returns 1 when the variable is unset. `scaleDeadline` refuses a result outside the timer range. Only the scale configuration reads the variable, and only the workflow sets it. With factor 3, the largest deadline is 3,600,000 ms, inside the range, and the job timeout is 90 minutes.\n- The runner. It writes stdout and stderr to separate files and asks Vitest for a JSON report. A run exits 0 only when the child exits 0, the report holds exactly six unique cases in the four owners, and all six pass. A signal, a spawn error, or a missing or inconsistent report gives a nonzero exit. The upload step runs always, pins upload-artifact by commit and keeps the files for seven days. The workflow keeps read-only contents permission and uses no secret.\n- The tests. The two new Node cases cover default and factor-three deadlines, malformed factors, missing and duplicate results, and a real child that writes 3 MiB, a stderr line and six passing rows, then exits 1. The control removes only the exit propagation and fails only at the capture assertion, with exact restoration.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at f17b07a7: \"exit 0\". before.json and after.json are byte-equal. Both overrides stayed unset, so the six cases passed at their original deadlines. After the gate, only the note and two manifests change.\n- The evidence. The four manifests hash to the values that the note cites: c72399f7…, ba790205…, 797cb2d1… and aa2a1a41…. Their 51 entries match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match.\n\nThe note records the second main run, 42578225982, which passed all six cases with the original deadlines. The 30,000-entry case took 427 s there, against more than 600 s in the failed run. Both runs stay recorded, and neither proves a cause.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One helper sets each deadline from one value, and only the scale configuration supplies that value. The runner owns the workflow's output and its exit.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The runner spawns a fixed argument array with no shell. The workflow adds no permission or secret.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes:\n1. `scaleDeadline` falls back to factor 1 when `__ARTROOM_SCALE_DEADLINE_FACTOR__` is undefined. The scale configuration always defines it, so the fallback can only hide a define that never reached the Worker bundle. In that case the main run would use factor 1 without a sign. Throw instead. Every later gate then proves that the define reaches the four owners.\n2. The trigger list in scripts/scale-selection.mjs does not name scripts/scale-runner.mjs. A change to the runner alone does not select scale in the review gate. The gate never runs the runner, so only the main run checks it.\n\nThis approval authorizes no deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7